  "common": {
    "baseline": "FBC, renal and liver profile; DPD phenotype/genotype before first fluorouracil unless already tested. Moderate/severe renal impairment may falsely elevate uracil; consider genotype.",
    "interactions": "00660/00421/00427/00428 explicitly contraindicate combined brivudin/sorivudin/analogues and warn INR rise with warfarin, phenytoin levels. FLOX directs to current SmPC/databases. Do not infer every regimen explicitly lists pregnancy: FLOX excludes breastfeeding, pregnancy needs product information not falsely attributed to its exclusion list.",
    "hepatic_boundaries": "All five fluorouracil tables say bilirubin<85 AND AST<180 full; bilirubin>85 OR AST>180 contraindicated. Exactly85 or180 omitted: consultant review, not automatic full dose. Absolute units not ULN ratios. Moderate impairment initial reduction1/3, severe1/2, clinical decision.427/428 separately exclude severe liver impairment, which must override/reconcile the reduction table.",
    "disease_monitoring": "All five defer imaging/tumour marker intervals to individual treatment plan; do not invent a universal fixed timetable.",
    "dpd": "Complete deficiency contraindicated; partial reduced starting dose/titration by consultant; unknown first-use status needs verification.",
    "consent": "Distinct intent/settings; include infection, bowel/mouth/skin toxicity, cardiac ischaemia, reproductive considerations, hypersensitivity; oxaliplatin-specific persistent neuropathy/cold dysaesthesia for FLOX; RT and vascular access risks for00421."
  },
